    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\n`Req.tail_str` can be called multiple times for the same request step, including during finish checks and streaming prefix checks. Cache the decoded tail string using `(len(output_ids), tail_len)` as the key so identical decodes within a step are performed only once.\r\n\r\nThe key changes when tokens are appended, retracted/reset, or multiple speculative tokens are accepted, so no explicit invalidation is required in those cases. When `output_ids` is rewritten in place without changing its length, clear the memo explicitly before finishing the request.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n- Memoize the most recently decoded tail string in `Req`.\r\n- Key the cache by `(len(output_ids), tail_len)`.\r\n- Reuse the cached value across finish and streaming prefix checks within the same step.\r\n- Clear the memo when `_check_vocab_boundary_finish` rewrites `output_ids` in place at the same length.\r\n- Preserve the existing decoding path and behavior for all other cases.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n**Passed**: Correctness verification completed.\r\n\r\n- All relevant stop-string and speculative decoding unit tests passed.\r\n- Baseline and candidate `finished_reason` and `finished_len` are identical.\r\n- Per-step `check_match_stop_str_prefix` results are identical.\r\n- Tested multi-token stop strings and partial-prefix cases.\r\n- Tested `stop_regex`.\r\n- Tested speculative multi-token appends.\r\n- Tested retraction-style reset.\r\n- Tested out-of-vocabulary tokens.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nPerformance improvement measured and verified on NVIDIA B300 SXM6.\r\n\r\n| Arm | n | Median | Unit |\r\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- |\r\n| Baseline | 10 | 14.8026 | us per request-step |\r\n| Candidate | 10 | 10.5604 | us per request-step |\r\n\r\n- Improvement: **28.66%**\r\n- Ratio: 0.7134\r\n- Hardware: NVIDIA B300 SXM6 PC x1\r\n- 10 trials per arm, 2 warmup trials, interleaved ABBA\r\n- Measurement threshold: 20%\r\n\r\nThe optimization removes one redundant tail-string decode per streaming stop-string request step. The absolute saving is approximately 3–7 us per request-step depending on tail length.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit\r\n- [x] Add unit tests\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy test results\r\n- [x] Provide speed benchmarks\r\n- [x] Code style compliance per SGLang guidelines\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36081226917](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081226917)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36081226582](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081226582)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36081226695](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36081226695)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
